  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary request path",
      "items": [
        "The browser authenticates with a local email/password session and posts a multipart screenshot; the API sanitizes it, stores the image and pending row, then returns 202.",
        "An in-process bounded job runs the pipeline; the pipeline reads the image, calls Gemini, optionally predicts local labels, and persists the result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust and input handling",
      "items": [
        "The client is outside the trusted application boundary; image size and decoded content are checked before storage.",
        "Gemini is an external boundary: the backend holds its API key and receives only validated metadata back. Local classification stays in the runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Runtime and persistence",
      "items": [
        "A DATABASE_URL selects Postgres for accounts, sessions, items, cache, usage and embeddings; without it the app uses local SQLite.",
        "Supabase Storage serves when configured; otherwise sanitized PNGs stay on local disk under opaque keys.",
        "The Ask agent rewrites follow-ups, routes retrieval and cites sources; classification is a challenger that cannot block an item from reaching ready."
      ]
    }
  ]
